  🆘 A problem document (RFC 9457): what an HTTP API says when it says no.

    📬 📝 🆕🆘 404❗️ 🔤No todo with that id🔤❗️❗️

  is a 404 whose body is

    {"type":"about:blank","title":"Not Found","status":404,"detail":"No todo with that id"}

  Every setter returns the problem, so they chain. The members are written in
  one order whatever order they were set in: type, title, status, detail,
  instance, extension members as they were added, errors. Type, title and
  status are always there; the rest only when set.

    🆕🆘 400❗️ ➡️ problem
    📝 problem 🔤The todo is not valid🔤❗️
    🚩 problem 🔤title🔤 🔤is required🔤❗️       💭 "errors":{"title":["is required"]}
